WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.690
Beijing, 1987.

2
00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:05.790
KFC opens its first restaurant in China.

3
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:11.830
By the end of 2025, there are
12,997 KFC restaurants in China,

4
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.890
in over 2,500 cities.

5
00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.610
And on the menu, beside the fried chicken:

6
00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:19.750
congee, a rice porridge.

7
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.090
Why would an American chicken
brand sell rice porridge?

8
00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:24.870
Does Chinese law require it?

9
00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:26.890
Is it a temporary promotion?

10
00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:30.730
In this mission, you'll find out
who actually runs KFC in China,

11
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.910
and where its fees flow.

12
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.630
Then you'll read two cultural landscapes:

13
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.630
a supertall tower in Cairo, and a
hand-carved temple in a London suburb.

14
00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.930
Your mission: explain why KFC
in China sells rice porridge.
